    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full build succeeded with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule *\"reject a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date \u2192 400\"* with minimal structural impact.\n\n**Changes (2 files):**\n\n1. **New class** `service/RegistrationDateValidator.java` \u2014 a tiny, cohesive unit (no surrounding class complexity) with one static method that throws `IllegalArgumentException` when the supplied date is after `LocalDate.now()`, and passes through `null`/valid dates unchanged.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` line routing `registrationDate` through the validator during `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`, matching the existing pattern used for `telephone`, `address`, and `postcode`.\n\n**Why this keeps cost low:** The existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already maps `IllegalArgumentException` \u2192 400, so no controller edit was needed \u2014 the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` and `Owner` classes (high WMC_other) were left untouched. The only edit is a one-line annotation on an abstract mapper method (CC 1), and the new logic lives in its own class with zero surrounding complexity.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` passes, full suite `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
